    <!--
        THE INVESTOR RELATIONS LEAD. Net new as of 2026-08-10 - no existing Lead carries this
        type and the backfill deliberately does not create any.

        SECURITY-LOAD-BEARING, same as the sibling type: the Lead_IR_Investor sharing rule is
        the only thing granting the Investor_Relations group access once Lead OWD is Private.

        NO APEX PATH CREATES THIS TYPE. The inbound email pipeline, the Broker Portal and lead
        conversion all stamp Acquisition_Broker explicitly. IR leads are created by hand or by
        a future IR intake that does not yet exist.

        ⚠ FIX 2026-08-10 (code review, CRITICAL) - EVERY PICKLIST ON THE OBJECT IS ENUMERATED
        BELOW - Salutation, GeocodeAccuracy, LeadSource, Status, Industry, Rating,
        Asset_Type__c, Broker_Priority__c, Deal_Type__c, Disqualification_Reason__c,
        Parse_Confidence__c and Sale_Process__c - because a record type file that omits a
        picklist silently drops ALL of that picklist's values from that type. This is the same
        rule already enforced under NDA__c, Contract_Review__c, Disposition__c and LOI__c; the
        original brief that produced this file omitted it, which was a plan defect, not a
        deliberate narrowing. The full value set was pulled from a LIVE ORG DESCRIBE
        (`sf sobject describe, sobject=Lead`), never from this repo's field files, because
        `sf project retrieve` unions local and remote picklist values and a repo field file can
        list values the org no longer has. Both Lead record types (this one and
        Acquisition_Broker) carry the IDENTICAL, COMPLETE value set with the SAME single default
        (Status = New) - narrowing either record type's values is a separate, deliberate change
        for later, and this fix is deliberately behaviour-neutral for every existing Lead. This
        type carries no existing rows today, so "behaviour-neutral" here means it is created
        with the full value set available from day one, matching its sibling.

        ⚠ FIX ROUND 2 (2026-08-10, check-only dry-run against usman-dpeg, deploy id
        0Afiw000000HR8fCAG) - added <businessProcess>Lead_Process</businessProcess>. Lead,
        Opportunity, Case and Solution record types each REQUIRE a BusinessProcess - a platform
        rule, confirmed by "Required field is missing: businessProcess" on this record type in
        the dry-run output. See objects/Lead/businessProcesses/Lead_Process.businessProcess-meta.xml
        for the full rationale, including why Status remains enumerated in BOTH places (this
        RecordType's own <picklistValues> AND the referenced BusinessProcess), and why one shared
        process serves both Lead record types rather than one each - it is the SAME process
        referenced by Acquisition_Broker, deliberately, so this must never diverge into a
        separate IR-only process without a fresh decision to do so.

        ⚠ FIX ROUND 3 (2026-08-10, iterative check-only dry-runs against usman-dpeg, root-caused
        by bisection on Contact/recordTypes/Broker.recordType-meta.xml) - Salutation AND
        GeocodeAccuracy REMOVED. Both failed with a GENERIC "An unexpected error occurred...
        ErrorId..." rather than a clean field-level message. Root cause, confirmed by bisection
        on the Contact sibling case (identical shape, cheaper to isolate there): both are
        COMPOUND-FIELD SUB-COMPONENTS - `compoundFieldName` in the live describe reads `Name`
        for Salutation and `Address` for GeocodeAccuracy - and every field that failed had this
        set while every field that passed did not. RecordType.picklistValues cannot restrict a
        compound field's sub-picklist; the platform does not report this as a clean validation
        error, it throws generically instead. THE RULE FOR ALL FUTURE TASKS IN THIS PLAN: a
        picklist that is a compound-field sub-component must NEVER be enumerated in a
        RecordType's picklistValues - check `compoundFieldName` in the describe, not just
        `type`, before adding any field to this file. The remaining TEN picklists below
        (LeadSource, Status, Industry, Rating, Asset_Type__c, Broker_Priority__c, Deal_Type__c,
        Disqualification_Reason__c, Parse_Confidence__c, Sale_Process__c) were each dry-run-
        validated (via the sibling Acquisition_Broker.recordType-meta.xml, identical value set)
        and remain enumerated identically on both Lead record types.
        [SUPERSEDED 2026-08-14: the count is now ELEVEN - see FIX ROUND 4 below. Everything
        else in this paragraph still stands.]

        FIX ROUND 4 (2026-08-14, Phase 1 re-review finding C4, CRITICAL) - Listing_Status__c
        ADDED, identically to the sibling Acquisition_Broker. It is the eleventh picklist and
        was the ONLY custom picklist on Lead missing from either Lead record type file. The
        field is created by P1-A of the acquisition-observations pack, and the brief that
        created it did not carry the FIX 2026-08-10 rule forward.

        WHY THIS TYPE TOO, WHEN NO IR LEAD IS EVER GATED. The blocking consequence described in
        the sibling file is an ACQUISITIONS one - Deal_Facts_Required_For_Under_Review and the
        inbound pipeline both belong to Acquisition_Broker, and no Apex path creates an IR lead
        at all. The reason this file gets the value anyway is the standing rule stated in the
        FIX 2026-08-10 paragraph above: both Lead record types carry the IDENTICAL, COMPLETE
        value set, and narrowing either one is a separate, deliberate change. Omitting it here
        would be exactly such a narrowing, taken by accident, and it would make the two files
        disagree for the first time. Do not "optimise" it back out.

        THE DROP-ON-OMISSION RULE IS REPO-ASSERTED, NOT MEASURED IN THIS ORG - see the sibling
        file's FIX ROUND 4, and agent-output/runbook-acquisition-observations-phase1.md section 1,
        heading "C4 (re-review, 2026-08-14)", for the cheap falsification. This edit is free if
        the assertion is wrong and load-bearing on the sibling if it is right.

        SHAPE. Both values, no default, matching the field's own valueSetDefinition order
        (On Market, Off Market; sorted=false). Listing_Status__c is a plain custom picklist with
        no compoundFieldName, so FIX ROUND 3's prohibition does not apply.

        DEPLOY ORDER. Must not be deployed before P1-A, which creates Lead.Listing_Status__c.
        P1-A already precedes P1-D1, where this file ships.
    -->
